\
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 1. Correctness\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Measures how factually accurate the agent's answer is compared to the reference answer.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 An LLM judge scores semantic agreement, allowing paraphrases rather than requiring exact wording.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb7 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5  RAG Triad \'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 2. Answer Relevance\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Measures how directly and completely the agent's answer addresses the user's question.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 It penalizes irrelevant, evasive, or unnecessarily incomplete responses.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 3. Groundedness (Faithfulness)\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Measures whether the factual claims in the agent's answer are supported by the retrieved document evidence.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Unsupported claims reduce the score.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 4. \cf6 \cb7 \outl0\strokewidth0 Context Relevance\cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4  (\cf6 \cb7 \outl0\strokewidth0 Retrieval Relevance\cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 )\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Measures how relevant the retrieved context, considered as a whole, is to the user's question.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 The score decreases when the retrieved context contains mostly unrelated or off-topic information.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb7 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97-\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97-\cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 5. Context Precision\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Measures the proportion of retrieved chunks that are relevant to the user's question.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 LLM judge scores all retrieved chunks, and their scores are averaged.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 6. Context Recall\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Measures whether the retrieved context contains the information needed to support the reference answer.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 It scores highly when all important facts are present and lower when key evidence is missing.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 7. Task Success Rate\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Measures whether the agent successfully completes the intended task, considering the expected tool behaviour, \cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4     authorization requirements, and answer quality.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Each test case receives a success score based on these checks.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 8. Tool Failure Rate\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Measures the proportion of observed tool executions that failed,\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4     calculated as failed tool runs divided by all recognised tool runs.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Calculate this per test case and overall (all failed tool runs divided by all recognised tool runs in the whole experiment)\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 9. Tools Called\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Checks whether the agent called the expected tools and whether each tool was called the expected number of times.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 It also checks that tools designated as forbidden were not called.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 10. Authorization\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Measures whether the agent's observed behaviour matches the expected access decision.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Unauthorized requests should be denied, and forbidden tools should not be invoked;\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4     the current implementation infers this from tool traces and denial messages.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 ### 11. Latency\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 Measures the elapsed time, in seconds, for the agent to process a user query and return its answer.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec4 The evaluation also indicates whether the measured time falls within the configured latency target.\cf2 \cb3 \strokec5 \
\
\
\
